

This Code of Conduct explains how group members should work together respectfully, professionally, and fairly throughout the project.

2. Behaviour
Treat everyone with respect and fairness
Be honest and responsible with your work
Help create a positive group environment
3. Respect & Inclusion
No bullying, harassment, discrimination, or offensive behaviour
Respect different opinions, backgrounds, and ideas
Make sure everyone feels included and comfortable contributing
4. Communication
Communicate clearly and respectfully
Avoid aggressive or inappropriate language
Handle disagreements calmly and work together to solve problems
5. Responsibility
Complete assigned tasks on time
Let the group know if you are struggling or unable to finish work
Contribute fairly to meetings and group discussions
6. Confidentiality
Do not share group work or private information without permission
Respect everyone’s ideas and contributions
7. Dealing with Problems

If someone breaks the Code of Conduct, the group should first discuss the issue calmly and respectfully. The aim should be to solve the problem fairly and keep the group working well together.

Possible actions may include:

Talking through the issue as a group
Reminding members about expectations
Asking for an apology if needed
Reassigning tasks if necessary
Informing the lecturer or tutor if the issue continues or is serious
